{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "Bnu_dpwPGxu6UDAjX",
	"notes": "A Skitarii Vanguard: the close-range counterpart to the Skitarii Ranger (Adeptus Mechanicus/Templates/Skitarii Ranger.gct), built around the radium carbine and the ambient radiation field its support gear leaks. Point math: ST 12 (+20), DX 13 (+60), IQ 10 (+0), HT 12 (+20) = 100; advantages +93 (Combat Reflexes 15 + Auto-senses, Skitarii Pattern 14 + Augmetic Legs, Combat Pattern 29 + Respirator Plugs 5 + Subdermal Armour Plating (3 levels, DR 3) 15 + Noospheric Link 8 + Rad-Saturation Field's own near-zero net cost 1 + Skitarii Doctrina Imperatives' GCS-discounted effective 6 points, exactly as the Ranger template uses); disadvantages -72; skills +63. Mechanicus Rank is included disabled by default. Total 184 points: the same \"between Trained Soldier and Elite Human\" band as the Ranger. Weapons (radium carbine, etc.) are equipment, not covered here.\n",
	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "tnpsNmYdywKEdz2DE",
			"name": "ST",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Skitarii physical conditioning and augmetic reinforcement together produce a soldier stronger than an ordinary Guardsman.\n\nDesign: ST 12 (+2), 10 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 20,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "st",
					"amount": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tNz0tchASH4h9KsUR",
			"name": "DX",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Cybernetic reflex conditioning and constant live-fire drilling.\n\nDesign: DX 13 (+3), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 60,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "dx",
					"amount": 3
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tVWIhyZTWUfjuMqwj",
			"name": "IQ",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Average intelligence; Skitarii conditioning narrows initiative and affect, not raw intellect.\n\nDesign: IQ 10 (baseline), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 0
		},
		{
			"id": "tr3mU-GaoT80lx7xh",
			"name": "HT",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Augmetic reinforcement and conditioning produce real battlefield endurance.\n\nDesign: HT 12 (+2), 10 pts/level (B14).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 20,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "ht",
					"amount": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "twTCNWMX5TLOp677R",
			"name": "Combat Reflexes",
			"reference": "B43",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Drilled, doctrina-reinforced reactions under fire.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Combat Reflexes (B43), 15 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 15
		},
		{
			"id": "tFvfsWjdsIMjIpdvI",
			"name": "Auto-senses, Skitarii Pattern",
			"reference": "B60",
			"local_notes": "Infravision; Acute Vision +2 (a +2 to the Vision roll, applied by the sheet).\n\nLore: Vanguard close-range doctrine doesn't need the Ranger's long zoom train, so they're issued the cheaper standard-pattern auto-senses instead of Ballistic Auto-senses.\n\nDesign: Infravision (B60, 10) + Acute Vision +2 (B35, 2/level, 4) = 14 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"base_points": 14,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "vision",
					"amount": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tzsj64Xc01KHDfGsj",
			"name": "Augmetic Legs, Combat Pattern (Matched Pair)",
			"reference": "B46",
			"local_notes": "DR 6 on both legs; Basic Move +1 from servo-assisted stride.\n\nLore: Skitarii Rangers and Vanguard are routinely fielded with both legs replaced outright rather than one at a time; the matched pair's synchronized actuators give a longer, steadier stride than a single prosthetic bolted onto an otherwise natural gait.\n\nDesign: DR 6, Partial (both legs) -20% (6x5=30, x0.8=24) + Basic Move +1 (B17, 5 points/level) = 29 points. Buying only one leg from this pair does not grant the Move bonus; use Augmetic Leg, Menial Pattern for a single prosthetic instead.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus",
				"Skitarii"
			],
			"base_points": 29,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "dr_bonus",
					"locations": [
						"leg"
					],
					"amount": 6
				},
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "basic_move",
					"amount": 1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "t9i1J2o1gj4qxKhvB",
			"name": "Respirator Plugs (Filtration Lungs)",
			"reference": "B55",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Grille-covered intake valves set into the throat or chest, scrubbing forge smog, promethium fumes, and toxic industrial atmosphere before it reaches the lungs — near-universal among Mechanicus adepts who spend their working lives on a forge-world's surface.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Filter Lungs (B55), 5 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"base_points": 5
		},
		{
			"id": "tDin5ka9m1KYkY61W",
			"name": "Subdermal Armour Plating",
			"reference": "B46",
			"local_notes": "DR 1 per level, all locations (2 levels = DR 2); stacks with worn armor.\n\nLore: Ceramite or plasteel weave grafted beneath the skin across the whole body, rather than replacing a specific organ or limb — a whole-body counterpart to the Astartes' Ossmodula (which is DR 3 to torso and vitals only), bought by Tech-Priests who expect to take a hit.\n\nDesign: Plain Damage Resistance (B46), 5 points/level, no location restriction since it covers the whole body. Bought here at a default 2 levels (DR 2, 10 points); raise or lower the level to taste. The DR is a real per-level feature, so changing the level changes the sheet. Suggested levels: Magos 2-3, Skitarii 3, Servitor 4.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"points_per_level": 5,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 3,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "dr_bonus",
					"locations": [
						"all"
					],
					"amount": 1,
					"per_level": true
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tjZ0ukiE8tNiTo9qi",
			"name": "Noospheric Link",
			"reference": "B91",
			"local_notes": "Short-to-medium range wireless data-link to the Cult Mechanicus' noosphere: other Noospheric Link-bearing adepts and compatible cogitators/machine spirits only.\n\nLore: A subcutaneous vox-and-data transceiver that lets a Tech-Priest read and post to the layered, half-mystical data-cloud the Mechanicus calls the noosphere — status runes, binharic liturgy, and tactical chatter overlaid on the world for anyone plugged in, and gibberish static to anyone who isn't.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Telecommunication (Radio type, B91, 10 points) with the Racial limitation (B91, -20%, restricted to others who share the trait — here, other noosphere-linked adepts and machine spirits): 10 x 0.8 = 8 points. Pairs with Language (Binharic), below, for the liturgical cant spoken over the link; the link itself is the hardware, the language is the learned code riding on it.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"base_points": 8
		},
		{
			"id": "T6e_gYENx-l3I1dHz",
			"name": "Rad-Saturation Field",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Skitarii Vanguard carry radium weapons whose ammunition and support systems bleed a low but constant field of ionizing radiation, harmless to the fully-sealed Skitarii themselves in the short term but a real hazard to anyone standing near one unprotected — and, over a long enough campaign, a hazard to the Vanguard too, one more reason Skitarii service so rarely ends in old age.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Toxic) (B61, 4/die) with Aura (B102, an estimated +80%, so it affects everyone in reach without an attack roll), Always On (B110, an estimated -20%, it can't be switched off) and Emanation (B112, an estimated -20%, it can't be aimed or withheld from allies): net +40%, 4 x 1.4 = 5.6, rounded to 6. Paired with Unfit (B160, -5) for the field's slow toll on its own bearer. Net 1 point: deliberately close to zero, since this is simultaneously a minor hazard-weapon and a curse, not a purchase anyone takes for the points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Disadvantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus",
				"Skitarii"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "t6qs-TLMMyPZWXTKk",
					"name": "Ambient Radium Field",
					"reference": "B61",
					"local_notes": "Innate Attack (Toxic), 1 die, always on, affecting everyone adjacent (including allies) each turn they're in reach; HT to resist as normal for toxic damage.",
					"base_points": 6
				},
				{
					"id": "tVCb47w2Tz9IYfd47",
					"name": "Unfit",
					"reference": "B160",
					"local_notes": "The same field that saturates the air nearby also cooks its bearer slowly.",
					"base_points": -5
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "Trqh-X_4_F9yPg1E3",
			"name": "Skitarii Doctrina Imperatives",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Skitarii Maniple's cranial implants take a battle-doctrina uploaded before an engagement, biasing every Skitarii in the maniple toward one combat posture at a time: Protector (hold ground and shoot) or Conqueror (advance and shoot). The Codex names these two; the earlier draft's third, Hunter, is not in the sources this project could identify and has been dropped. A Skitarii can only run one imperative at a time and must be re-flashed (a Ready maneuver, or a scene break, at the GM's call) to switch.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Alternative Abilities (B61): buy the most expensive ability at full price and the rest at 1/5 cost (round up), since only one can be active. Full prices: Protector and Conqueror are each a narrow +1 combat Talent (B90-style, 5). GCS applies the Alternative Abilities discount natively for this container type; worked by hand, the effective total is 5 + ceil(5/5) = 6 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus",
				"Skitarii"
			],
			"container_type": "alternative_abilities",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tjn5IX2noZfpdKNE8",
					"name": "Protector Imperative",
					"reference": "B90",
					"local_notes": "+1 to Guns and Gunner skills when the Skitarii did not move this turn (Talent-style construction, holding position).",
					"base_points": 5
				},
				{
					"id": "tryAK8ywM8aPqZnHE",
					"name": "Conqueror Imperative",
					"reference": "B90",
					"local_notes": "+1 to Guns and Gunner skills when the Skitarii moved this turn (Talent-style construction, advancing fire).",
					"base_points": 5
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tnvrDYG4kDTTlqki3",
			"name": "Mechanicus Rank",
			"reference": "B29",
			"local_notes": "Levels: 1 Skitarii Alpha/menial overseer, 2-3 Enginseer, 4-5 Magos, 6-7 Archmagos, 8 Fabricator-Locum, 9 Fabricator-General of a Forge World.\n\nLore: Disabled by default: most Vanguard hold no formal Mechanicus rank at all. Enable at level 1 (+5 points) for a Skitarii Alpha or veteran squad leader.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Rank (B29), 5 points/level, by direct analogy with this project's existing Military Rank and Religious Rank entries (Imperium/Traits/Imperial Traits.adq).",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"points_per_level": 5,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 1,
			"max_levels": 9,
			"disabled": true
		},
		{
			"id": "TMjIFbf40ycy5Xp2c",
			"name": "Skitarii Conditioning",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Skitarii undergo extensive neural conditioning and cybernetic replacement of their own that, while far short of a Servitor's total lobotomy, strips away most of the emotional affect and small-talk that would otherwise mark them as still fully human — codex and Black Library background alike describe them as unnervingly flat and literal even next to other Mechanicus adepts.\n\nDesign: Low Empathy (B142, -20) + No Sense of Humor (B146, -10) + a 1-point Quirk (B9) for clipped, ritualized speech patterns = -31 points. Deliberately short of Servitor Lobotomy (Neural Excision) above: Skitarii still hold rank, opinions, and (per some Codex background) occasional flickers of the person they were, where a Servitor has none of that left.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus",
				"Skitarii"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "t9CQZAQx2T7YhwZU4",
					"name": "Low Empathy",
					"reference": "B142",
					"base_points": -20
				},
				{
					"id": "tB2N-ySnumVccppNq",
					"name": "No Sense of Humor",
					"reference": "B146",
					"base_points": -10
				},
				{
					"id": "tqH2scQBCk-Wwun7A",
					"name": "Speaks Only in Clipped Binharic-Inflected Report",
					"tags": [
						"Quirk"
					],
					"base_points": -1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tiHg8W59LUCMjiiMM",
			"name": "Fanaticism (The Omnissiah)",
			"reference": "B136",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Doctrinal certainty that the Machine God — the same Emperor, in the Cult Mechanicus' own theology, understood as a being of pure technological perfection — must be served without question, and that His will (as interpreted by the Priesthood's hierarchy) justifies whatever it demands. Distinct from the Imperial Creed's Fanaticism (The God-Emperor) in Imperium/Traits/Imperial Traits.adq: the same shape of belief, aimed at a different reading of the same divinity.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Fanaticism (B136), flat -15, as the existing Imperial Fanaticism entry is built.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"base_points": -15
		},
		{
			"id": "tJvajVX0K5yjl56I5",
			"name": "Duty (Adeptus Mechanicus)",
			"reference": "B133",
			"local_notes": "Overridden to -15 (almost always hazardous) rather than this trait's -10 baseline: a Skitarii's Duty is combat service, not a workshop posting.\n\nLore: A sworn Tech-Priest, Enginseer, or Skitarii answers first to their Forge World and its Fabricator-General, not to any Guard officer or Administratum functionary they happen to be attached to — a binding, frequent, but not universally life-threatening obligation (unlike a Guardsman's), since a Mechanicus posting is at least as often archival or industrial as it is a battlefield one.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Duty (B133), fairly frequent but not \"almost always hazardous\" the way Duty (Astra Militarum) is (Imperium/Traits/ Imperial Traits.adq) — pegged one tier below that entry, at -10, to reflect the Priesthood's broader range of postings. A Skitarii or a field-attached Enginseer/Techmarine should reasonably use -15 instead; -10 is this template's baseline for a workshop- or forge-based adept.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"base_points": -15
		},
		{
			"id": "tHuizX8mZ6ByAFz2J",
			"name": "Intolerance (Xenos)",
			"reference": "B140",
			"local_notes": "Lore: \"The alien is the enemy\" as baseline Imperial doctrine — not personal bigotry but state religion. Universal across Black Library fiction; only a minority of xenos-sympathetic characters (some Rogue Traders, Ordo Xenos radicals) lack it.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Intolerance (B140). Costed at -10, the \"very broad category\" end of the range the book allows, since \"all non-human sapient species\" is about as broad a target as Intolerance can name.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		},
		{
			"id": "tCGt3qD-F77mUYhsY",
			"name": "Doesn't Question a Doctrina Imperative",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Skitarii obeys the uploaded battle-doctrina without hesitation, for good or ill.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only.",
			"tags": [
				"Quirk",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -1
		}
	],
	"skills": [
