		{
			"id": "sr-SaPt_fmfnDbV4t",
			"name": "Stealth",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Enough fieldcraft to close to radium-carbine range; less emphasized than a Ranger's overwatch discipline, so bought at half the level.\n\nDesign: DX+0 (13) for 4 points, Average.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/a",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "sJqACk7VxY_2y98uK",
			"name": "Camouflage",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Breaking up a firing position's silhouette.\n\nDesign: IQ+0 (10) for 1 point, Easy.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"difficulty": "iq/e",
			"points": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "scKHPoZWh1ezGt8dp",
			"name": "Survival",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Field survival in whatever terrain the maniple is deployed to.\n\nDesign: Per+0 (10) for 2 points, Average.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"specialization": "(choose deployment terrain)",
			"difficulty": "per/a",
			"points": 2
		},
		{
			"id": "sFViWtvA5G6kUvTxO",
			"name": "Brawling",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Vanguard close to contact range far more often than Rangers do, and are drilled accordingly in melee back-up skill.\n\nDesign: DX+1 (14) for 4 points, Easy.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/e",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "sawqDmeYrIoYUrgpi",
			"name": "Forced Entry",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Breaching doors and barricades in close-quarters actions.\n\nDesign: DX+1 (14) for 2 points, Easy.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/e",
			"points": 2
		},
		{
			"id": "skZ6_HQZJ-V6AC3HP",
			"name": "Theology",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Vanguard's basic catechisms of the Machine God; see Imperium/Skills/Imperial Skills.skl.\n\nDesign: IQ-1 (9) for 4 points, Hard.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"specialization": "Cult Mechanicus",
			"difficulty": "iq/h",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "sPvbJ6XQ514mA66Zu",
			"name": "Savoir-Faire",
			"reference": "B218",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Court protocol inside the Priesthood: correct forms of address for a Magos or Archmagos, ritual precedence between Forge Worlds and Explorator fleets, and which questions are simply never asked of a superior adept. Not attested under this exact name in the fiction, but the Mechanicus is consistently shown (across Black Library and codex background) to run on a court culture at least as rigid as the Ecclesiarchy's own.\n\nDesign: IQ+0 (10) for 1 point, Easy.",
			"tags": [
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"specialization": "Adeptus Mechanicus",
			"difficulty": "iq/e",
			"defaults": [
				{
					"type": "iq",
					"modifier": -4
				}
			],
			"points": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "sZb3Y0XX6TlqI1G9s",
			"name": "Intimidation",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A visibly rad-scarred Vanguard is a frightening thing to stand near.\n\nDesign: Will+0 (10) for 2 points, Average.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"difficulty": "will/a",
			"points": 2
		},
		{
			"id": "sxejCx9CWzlLyuWMu",
			"name": "First Aid",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Basic combat first aid.\n\nDesign: IQ+0 (10) for 1 point, Easy.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"difficulty": "iq/e",
			"points": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "sbb9nZoslIFFfiVSh",
			"name": "Climbing",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Assault-position fitness.\n\nDesign: DX-1 (12) for 1 point, Average.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/a",
			"points": 1
		},
		{
